Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement. Question: When are the representations and warranties required to be made according to the bring down provision? Option A: At Closing Only  Option B: At Signing & At Closing

Merger Agreement: Section 8.1 Conditions to Completion. Notwithstanding any prior representations, the representations and warranties set forth in the Company’s Schedule A are initially affirmed as of the Execution Date of this Agreement. However, the representation contained in Paragraph 2.5(b) shall be re-affirmed at the Closing, without any reliance on the Execution Date valuation. Moreover, all other representations and warranties provided in Articles II and III are deemed to have remained true from the Execution Date through to the Closing, subject to the standard materiality threshold as defined in Section 3.2. (Page 119)
