Instruction: Read the segment of an acquisition agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the timing requirement for the representations and warranties.\nQuestion: Under the bring down provision in this agreement, when must the representations and warranties be accurate?\nOption A: They must be accurate only as of the Closing Date.\nOption B: They must be accurate both at the time of signing and again at the Closing Date.\n\nAcquisition Agreement Excerpt: Section 12. Confirmations and Accuracy. The parties agree that all representations and warranties set forth in this Agreement shall be true and correct as of the date of signing, notwithstanding limited de minimis variations which do not, individually or in aggregate, materially affect the transaction. Furthermore, these representations and warranties are required to be reconfirmed as of the Closing Date, with no reliance on any prior materiality thresholds, except where a specific date is expressly referenced in a particular clause. In such cases, any deviation beyond nominal discrepancies will trigger the bring down verification process at both stages. (Page 112)
